  "interpretation": [
    "The unchanged primary metric measures exact normalized written-transcript agreement; it does not separate acoustic recognition from choice of writing system, spelling or written number conventions.",
    "Cyrillic output against a Latin reference is penalized even if some content could be equivalent. No transliteration was attempted, so the magnitude of a hypothetical script-normalized score is unknown.",
    "All745 publisher references use Latin letters. Whisper has Cyrillic letters in63 outputs (8.4564%), but10,148 of10,968 total word edits occur in its670 Latin-only outputs. Therefore the measured error count is not predominantly located in cross-script outputs. This is exhaustive descriptive accounting, not an alternative subset WER.",
    "Latin-only outputs also contain visible word/spelling differences in the source-order examples. The entire observed gap cannot be declared a script effect from these descriptive counts.",
    "WER above100% is possible because insertions contribute errors in addition to substitutions and deletions; it does not mean100% failed requests.",
    "Whisper used the known uz language token, but that token does not guarantee Latin-script output in these recorded results. This is an observation of outputs, not a language-support or causal diagnosis.",
    "Empty counts follow the unchanged scorer: Whisper has8 outputs empty after normalization, of which7 are raw empty strings; one punctuation-only output also normalizes to empty."
